---
{
  title: "ignore_rejection"
}
---
### NAME

    ignore_rejection() - Returns a do-nothing rejection handler owned by the
    simul_efun object.

### SYNOPSIS

    function ignore_rejection( void );

### DESCRIPTION

    Returns a do-nothing rejection handler owned by the simul_efun object.

    For marking a promise's rejection as observed when the object that
    started the work may not be alive to observe it. A handler written in
    the caller cannot do this job: a funptr belongs to the object that
    created it, so when that object is destructed the handler is destructed
    with it and the rejection it was meant to take goes unhandled anyway --
    reported as "Owner of function pointer is destructed" rather than as the
    original reason. This one outlives every caller.

    Use it only where the rejection genuinely needs no action, the usual
    case being an async body abandoned because its own object went away.

### RETURN VALUES

    (function) A handler that ignores its argument and returns 0.

### EXAMPLE

    {{di1}}// The flow is moot if the connection drops while it is parked.
    promise_catch(login_flow(), ignore_rejection());{{di0}}
